// App granted Defender API permissions
//
// Fires when an app gets permissions on the Defender for Endpoint API. Some of those
// permissions can run Live Response or isolate any device, so treat it like someone adding
// an admin.
//
// Runs:      Continuous (NRT)
// Severity:  High
// MITRE:     T1098
// Tables:    CloudAppEvents
//
// Needs:
//   - The Defender for Cloud Apps Microsoft 365 connector with Microsoft 365 activities
//     turned on.
//   - Entra events show up in CloudAppEvents with a trailing dot on the action name, which
//     is why the query matches on the start of it.
//
// Triage (paste into Recommended actions):
//   - Check which app, which permission (AppRole.Value in RawEventData), who granted it,
//     and the ticket.
//   - Escalate if there's no ticket, or the permission covers Live Response, isolation or
//     indicators.
//   - Close if it's a ticketed integration. Write down the app and its owner.

CloudAppEvents
| where ingestion_time() > ago(1d)
| where ActionType startswith "Add app role assignment to service principal"
| where tostring(RawEventData) contains "fc780465-2017-40d4-a0c5-307022471b92" or tostring(RawEventData) has "WindowsDefenderATP"
| project Timestamp, ReportId, AccountObjectId, AccountDisplayName, IPAddress, ActionType, RawEventData
